WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.068
-Hello and welcome, welcome,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.036
welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody!

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:08.040
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.643
Well, guys, next week,
President Trump is planning

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.812
to leave the White House
for Palm Beach

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.047
on the morning
of Inauguration Day

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:16.649
and he's asked
for a large crowd

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.018
and a big,
military-style sendoff.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.219
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.689
Yeah.
Trump wants a big farewell.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.725
He's even requested
a red carpet, live music,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.860
and Rudy Giuliani
to be launched from a cannon.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.462
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.397
It's going to be quite a day.
A bunch of Trump supporters

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:32.565
in Washington, D.C.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.633
What could possibly go wrong?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.101
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.436
That's right, Trump wants
to assemble a large crowd

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.505
to remind everyone
of his legacy --

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.274
completely ignoring
the coronavirus.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:45.378
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.181
Trump's basically
that annoying friend

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.350
who keeps dropping hints that
they want a surprise party.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.951
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.286
[ As Trump ]
Can't believe Wednesday is

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.554
my last day.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.223
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.093
And I've been really getting
into listening to vinyl records.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:04.130
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.800
Yep, Trump wants a big send-off,
but, as of now,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.300
the only thing they have planned

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.603
is an awkward office party
with a cake that says...

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.773
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:17.677
Yeah, Trump is expecting
a big military presence.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.778
Officials would be like,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.513
"Yes, sir, the, uh,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.982
Space Force is doing
a s-space parade.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.984
You just can't see it from here.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.252
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.820
Apparently, Trump wants
all his favorite

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.088
military officials
to be there --

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.290
generals, colonels,
captains, admirals.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.359
I think we actually
have a photo.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.460
Yeah, there you go.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.097
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:41.000
Imagine what he'd ask for
if he won the election.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.335
[ As Trump ]
I wanted stealth fighters.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.170
I want zebras.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.673
I want a cement truck
demolition derby.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.073
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:50.176
Really been getting
into vinyl records.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.277
[ Laughter ]
Listening.

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:54.814
This is interesting --
since Biden and Trump will be

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.649
in different places
for the inauguration,

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.686
they each will have a suitcase
holding the nuclear codes.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.555
But, once Biden takes the oath,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.258
Trump's codes will deactivate.
Yeah.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.894
What's crazy is that the guy
we don't trust to be on Twitter

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.596
is still carrying around
the nuclear codes.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.331
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.065
There's no way
Trump still has a briefcase

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:14.367
with the actual nuclear codes.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.135
I'm sure, years ago,
someone switched it out

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.304
with one of the briefcases
from "Deal or No Deal"

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.039
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.440
[ As Trump ]
32.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.342
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.078
Meanwhile, I heard that Trump
is still deciding

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.413
whether he'll carry on
the presidential tradition

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.215
of writing a letter
to his successor

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.951
and leaving it
on the Resolute Desk.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.386
I'm not sure how much wisdom
Trump has to offer.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.356
So far, Trump's only
"advice" to Biden is

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.691
to call dibs on the
Lincoln Bedroom before Jill.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.495
"No, no, we actually
sleep in the same --"

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.297
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.632
My guess is,
instead of a letter,

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.233
Trump's going to pull
a "Sex and the City"

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.668
and leave a Post-It that says...

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.239
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.841
But this is nice --
Melania is leaving Jill Biden

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.810
the same letter Michelle Obama
left for her.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.878
Isn't that sweet?

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.681
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.216
[ Applause ]
Isn't that sweet?

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.351
Speaking of Biden moving
into the White House,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.052
there are reports
that he may have to leave

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:09.088
his Peloton bike behind,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.756
since it has a camera
and microphone

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.625
that could be hacked.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.993
Even hackers were like,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.328
[ Slavic accent ]
"If you think we want to watch

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.729
old man sweat and grunt

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.197
to REO Speedwagon,

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.532
you're very mistaken."

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.966
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.269
Actually, I forgot
the White House even had a gym.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.637
For the last four years,
it's just been a place

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.738
to hide from the president.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.707
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.741
Some sports news --
the NFL playoffs

00:03:29.741 --> 00:03:31.010
continue this weekend

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.779
and one matchup everyone
is excited about is

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.114 line:0%
Tom Brady versus Drew Brees,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.649 line:0%
the two oldest quarterbacks
in the league.

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:38.951
They're already wishing
each other good luck.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.154
Today, Brady called Brees
and was like, "Break a hip."

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.422
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:45.291
Yeah, instead of Bud Light
and Doritos commercials,

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.592
there are going to be just
a bunch of commercials

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:47.760 line:0%
for the UroClub.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.231 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.567
-Hell!

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.970
-Yeah, those guys are so old,
when they see Patrick Mahomes,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.071
they just pinch his cheeks.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.505
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.173
Alright, listen to this --
I saw is

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:04.376
the 20th anniversary
of Wikipedia.

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:05.578
At least, I think it is.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.780
I'm not sure because I read it
on Wikipedia.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.448
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:10.816
It's amazing --
in just 20 years,

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:13.453
Wikipedia has written
20 trillion high school essays.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.988
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.657
Meanwhile, Tom Brady
and Drew Brees were like,

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.458
"Back in my day,
if we want to know something,

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:20.793
we had to Ask Jeeves."

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.595
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.197
And, finally,
police in Argentina

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:27.099
raided a swingers party,
but, when they showed up,

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:29.167
the swingers thought
the cops were strippers.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:32.538
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.574
It didn't help when the cops
were like, "Alright,

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.808
we can do this the easy way

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.577
or the hard way."
[ Laughter ]

